    },
    "mathematics": {
      "verdict": "pass",
      "independent_solution": "Both graphs have real domain x!=0, range y!=0, two branches and asymptotes x=0 and y=0, with no axis points. The first has xy=6 in quadrants I/III and contains (2,3),(-2,-3). The second has xy=-12 in quadrants II/IV and contains (3,-4),(-3,4). Only A states all these facts. B instead describes products -6 and +12. C includes two valid positive-x sample points but omits the negative-x branches. D gets the qualitative facts right but its pairs have products +60 and -120, not +6 and -12. The complete true set is {A}.",
      "correct": ["A"],
      "option_checks": [
        {
          "option_id": "A",
          "truth": "correct",
          "evidence": "2*3=(-2)*(-3)=6 and 3*(-4)=(-3)*4=-12. Both sign-symmetric branches are in the stated quadrants. Both axes are asymptotes and neither axis belongs to either nonzero-product graph."
        },
